{'review': '{\n  "review": "<<<ARTIFACT review_report>>>\\n{\\"overall_status\\":\\"NEEDS_FIXES\\",\\"quality_score\\":6.5,\\"summary\\":{\\"critical\\":0,\\"high\\":1,\\"medium\\":3,\\"low\\":3,\\"passed_checks\\":[\\"No hardcoded secrets\\",\\"Proper cleanup in useEffect\\",\\"TypeScript typings\\"]},\\"findings\\":[{\\"finding_id\\":\\"F-001\\",\\"severity\\":\\"medium\\",\\"category\\":\\"security\\",\\"title\\":\\"Access token exposed in URL query string and console logs\\",\\"file\\":\\"src/hooks/useWebSocket.ts\\",\\"line_range\\":[43,44],\\"description\\":\\"The access token is appended as a query parameter to the WebSocket URL and logged in plain text, potentially exposing it to server logs, browser history, or network traces.\\",\\"impact\\":\\"Token leakage could lead to unauthorized WebSocket connections and potential account compromise.\\",\\"suggested_fix\\":\\"Avoid logging the full URL with token. Use encodeURIComponent for the token value and consider alternative authentication mechanisms (e.g., subprotocol) if available.\\",\\"code_before\\":\\"    const wsUrlWithToken = `${url}?access_token=${accessToken}`;\\\\n    console.log(`Attempting to connect to WebSocket: ${wsUrlWithToken}`);\\",\\"code_after\\":\\"    const wsUrlWithToken = `${url}?access_token=${encodeURIComponent(accessToken)}`;\\\\n    console.log(`Attempting to connect to WebSocket: ${url}`); // token omitted from log\\",\\"references\\":[\\"OWASP A02:2021 – Cryptographic Failures\\",\\"https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/\\"]},{\\"finding_id\\":\\"F-002\\",\\"severity\\":\\"medium\\",\\"category\\":\\"quality\\",\\"title\\":\\"Missing URL encoding for access token\\",\\"file\\":\\"src/hooks/useWebSocket.ts\\",\\"line_range\\":[43,43],\\"description\\":\\"The access token is directly interpolated into the URL without encoding. If the token contains characters such as ?, &, =, or spaces, the resulting URL may be malformed.\\",\\"impact\\":\\"WebSocket connection may fail unexpectedly due to invalid URL.\\",\\"suggested_fix\\":\\"Encode the access token using encodeURIComponent before appending to the URL.\\",\\"code_before\\":\\"    const wsUrlWithToken = `${url}?access_token=${accessToken}`;\\",\\"code_after\\":\\"    const wsUrlWithToken = `${url}?access_token=${encodeURIComponent(accessToken)}`;\\",\\"references\\":[]},{\\"finding_id\\":\\"F-003\\",\\"severity\\":\\"high\\",\\"category\\":\\"quality\\",\\"title\\":\\"Callback dependencies cause unnecessary reconnect loops\\",\\"file\\":\\"src/hooks/useWebSocket.ts\\",\\"line_range\\":[28,76],\\"description\\":\\"The connect useCallback depends on onOpen, onMessage, onError, onClose. If these callbacks are recreated on each render (common when defined inline in a component), the connect callback will be recreated, causing the useEffect to re-run and potentially disconnect/reconnect repeatedly.\\",\\"impact\\":\\"Unstable WebSocket connection, excessive reconnection attempts, and performance degradation.\\",\\"suggested_fix\\":\\"Use useRef to store the latest callback versions, or wrap callbacks in useRef and call the ref\'s current inside connect. Then remove the callback functions from connect\'s dependency array.\\",\\"code_before\\":\\"  const connect = useCallback(() => {\\\\n    // ... uses onOpen, onMessage, onError, onClose\\\\n  }, [url, accessToken, onOpen, onMessage, onError, onClose, reconnectInterval, reconnectLimit]);\\",\\"code_after\\":\\"  const onOpenRef = useRef(onOpen);\\\\n  const onMessageRef = useRef(onMessage);\\\\n  const onErrorRef = useRef(onError);\\\\n  const onCloseRef = useRef(onClose);\\\\n  useEffect(() => {\\\\n    onOpenRef.current = onOpen;\\\\n    onMessageRef.current = onMessage;\\\\n    onErrorRef.current = onError;\\\\n    onCloseRef.current = onClose;\\\\n  }, [onOpen, onMessage, onError, onClose]);\\\\n\\\\n  const connect = useCallback(() => {\\\\n    // ... same body but use onOpenRef.current etc.\\\\n  }, [url, accessToken, reconnectInterval, reconnectLimit]);\\",\\"references\\":[\\"React Hooks FAQ: Why am I seeing stale props or state inside my callback?\\",\\"https://reactjs.org/docs/hooks-faq.html#why-am-i-seeing-stale-props-or-state-inside-my-callback\\"]},{\\"finding_id\\":\\"F-004\\",\\"severity\\":\\"medium\\",\\"category\\":\\"quality\\",\\"title\\":\\"Returning ws.current instead of the ref leads to stale closure\\",\\"file\\":\\"src/hooks/useWebSocket.ts\\",\\"line_range\\":[106,106],\\"description\\":\\"The returned ws property is the current value of the ref at render time. If the WebSocket is recreated after a render, the returned ws value will not update, causing stale references.\\",\\"impact\\":\\"Consumers of the hook may send messages to a closed WebSocket or miss connection state changes.\\",\\"suggested_fix\\":\\"Return the ref object itself (ws) so consumers can access ws.current for the latest value, or provide a function that returns ws.current.\\",\\"code_before\\":\\"  return { ws: ws.current, isConnected, message, sendMessage, connect, disconnect };\\",\\"code_after\\":\\"  return { ws, isConnected, message, sendMessage, connect, disconnect };\\",\\"references\\":[]},{\\"finding_id\\":\\"F-005\\",\\"severity\\":\\"low\\",\\"category\\":\\"quality\\",\\"title\\":\\"Missing validation for reconnectInterval and reconnectLimit\\",\\"file\\":\\"src/hooks/useWebSocket.ts\\",\\"line_range\\":[18,19],\\"description\\":\\"The hook accepts reconnectInterval and reconnectLimit options but does not validate that they are non‑negative numbers. Negative or zero values could cause infinite loops or immediate reconnect attempts.\\",\\"impact\\":\\"Misconfiguration may lead to busy‑loop reconnection attempts or excessive resource consumption.\\",\\"suggested_fix\\":\\"Add validation: ensure reconnectInterval > 0 and reconnectLimit >= 0, falling back to sensible defaults if invalid.\\",\\"code_before\\":\\"    reconnectInterval = 3000,\\\\n    reconnectLimit = 5,\\",\\"code_after\\":\\"    reconnectInterval = Number.isFinite(options?.reconnectInterval) && options.reconnectInterval > 0 ? options.reconnectInterval : 3000,\\\\n    reconnectLimit = Number.isFinite(options?.reconnectLimit) && options.reconnectLimit >= 0 ? options.reconnectLimit : 5,\\",\\"references\\":[]},{\\"finding_id\\":\\"F-006\\",\\"severity\\":\\"low\\",\\"category\\":\\"quality\\",\\"title\\":\\"Risk of state updates on unmounted component\\",\\"file\\":\\"src/hooks/useWebSocket.ts\\",\\"line_range\\":[49,56],\\"description\\":\\"The onopen and onmessage handlers call setIsConnected and setMessage without checking if the component is still mounted. If the component unmounts before the WebSocket event fires, React will warn about state updates on an unmounted component.\\",\\"impact\\":\\"Memory warnings and potential race conditions.\\",\\"suggested_fix\\":\\"Use a ref to track mount state and check it before calling state setters.\\",\\"code_before\\":\\"    ws.current.onopen = (event) => {\\\\n      console.log(\\"WebSocket connected.\\");\\\\n      setIsConnected(true);\\\\n      reconnectAttempts.current = 0;\\\\n      onOpen?.(event);\\\\n    };\\\\n\\\\n    ws.current.onmessage = (event) => {\\\\n      setMessage(event.data);\\\\n      onMessage?.(event);\\\\n    };\\",\\"code_after\\":\\"  const isMounted = useRef(false);\\\\n  useEffect(() => {\\\\n    isMounted.current = true;\\\\n    return () => {\\\\n      isMounted.current = false;\\\\n    };\\\\n  }, []);\\\\n\\\\n    ws.current.onopen = (event) => {\\\\n      if (isMounted.current) {\\\\n        setIsConnected(true);\\\\n        reconnectAttempts.current = 0;\\\\n      }\\\\n      console.log(\\"WebSocket connected.\\");\\\\n      onOpen?.(event);\\\\n    };\\\\n\\\\n    ws.current.onmessage = (event) => {\\\\n      if (isMounted.current) {\\\\n        setMessage(event.data);\\\\n      }\\\\n      onMessage?.(event);\\\\n    };\\",\\"references\\":[]},{\\"finding_id\\":\\"F-007\\",\\"severity\\":\\"low\\",\\"category\\":\\"quality\\",\\"title\\":\\"onMessage handler assumes string data\\",\\"file\\":\\"src/hooks/useWebSocket.ts\\",\\"line_range\\":[54,56],\\"description\\":\\"The handler sets message state to event.data directly. WebSocket messages can be binary (Blob or ArrayBuffer), which would cause the state to be set to a non‑string value, potentially breaking consumers that expect a string.\\",\\"impact\\":\\"Incorrect state type leading to runtime errors in consumer components.\\",\\"suggested_fix\\":\\"Check the typeof event.data (or instanceof Blob/ArrayBuffer) and handle binary data appropriately—either ignore, convert to base64, or store in a separate state.\\",\\"code_before\\":\\"    ws.current.onmessage = (event) => {\\\\n      setMessage(event.data);\\\\n      onMessage?.(event);\\\\n    };\\",\\"code_after\\":\\"    ws.current.onmessage = (event) => {\\\\n      if (typeof event.data === \'string\') {\\\\n        setMessage(event.data);\\\\n      }\\\\n      // Optionally handle binary data:\\\\n      // if (event.data instanceof Blob) { /* ... */ }\\\\n      onMessage?.(event);\\\\n    };\\",\\"references\\":[]}],\\"positive_observations\\":[\\"Proper cleanup of WebSocket and timeouts in the useEffect return function\\",\\"Use of useCallback to prevent unnecessary re‑creations of connect/disconnect/sendMessage\\",\\"Clear reconnection logic with attempt limits and exponential backoff placeholder\\",\\"TypeScript interfaces provide good IntelliSense and safety\\"]}\\n<<<ENDARTIFACT>>>"\n}'}